From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vates Git Importer <gitimporter@vates.tech>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2015 07:09:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] SDEV_EVT_LUN_CHANGE_REPORTED events should only be reported
 when we're not expecting the LUN change. Lest it may trigger udev rules which
 in turn trigger more LUN change events.

Signed-off-by: Gerald Elder-Vass <gerald.elder-vass@cloud.com>
---
 drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c b/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
index e731af504f07..0ae411913217 100644
--- a/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
+++ b/drivers/scsi/scsi_error.c
@@ -418,7 +418,8 @@ static void scsi_report_sense(struct scsi_device *sdev,
 			sdev_printk(KERN_WARNING, sdev,
 				    "Inquiry data has changed");
 		} else if (sshdr->asc == 0x3f && sshdr->ascq == 0x0e) {
-			evt_type = SDEV_EVT_LUN_CHANGE_REPORTED;
+			if (!sdev->sdev_target->expecting_lun_change)
+				evt_type = SDEV_EVT_LUN_CHANGE_REPORTED;
 			scsi_report_lun_change(sdev);
 			sdev_printk(KERN_WARNING, sdev,
 				    "Warning! Received an indication that the "
